  {
    "sha": "5fef611a75c274901dc5cc2a350456179e27df7b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKDVmZWY2MTFhNzVjMjc0OTAxZGM1Y2MyYTM1MDQ1NjE3OWUyN2RmN2I",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T13:21:28Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T13:21:28Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): light theme gets a light viewport and inks that read on it\n\nThe 3D pass cleared to a fixed dark colour in every theme. The viewport\nground is now a theme token (light #DDE1E7, dark unchanged), and every\nink drawn over the viewport has a light-ground value tuned on screen:\ntoolpath moves and boundaries, wireframe, axes, overlays, the view cube\nand its buttons (with a centred, symmetric Axes triad), the corner hint\nand the playback tool marker.\n\nUnselected paths under \"Show all toolpaths\" fade toward a light ground\ninstead of scaling to near-black. Light-theme hover uses the viewport\ngrey with dark ink, window title bars wear the window fill instead of\negui's dark default, and the Debug info window draws its own title row\nwhose collapse and close buttons hover like the OS caption buttons.\nThe dark theme looks as before.\n\nFixes #698\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
